**Fix:** Add workflow.node.invoke to the step-kind lists in both docs and describe its node-invocation semantics.

### [MEDIUM] [prototypes-hygiene] .wzrrd/ contains machine-local publish state and is not gitignored

**Where:** `.wzrrd/state.json:1`

The untracked .wzrrd/ directory (state.json + a generated workflow-run-observability-pack/index.html, 44K) is machine-specific tool state: it embeds absolute /Users/joel/... source paths and live wzrrd.sh publish URLs. `git check-ignore .wzrrd/state.json` exits 1 — it is not ignored, so the next broad `git add .` commits this machine's publish ledger into the repo. The .keep file suggests intent, but state.json with absolute local paths does not belong in version control per the repo's own machine-specific-config norms.

**Evidence:** .wzrrd/state.json: '"source": "/Users/joel/Code/joelhooks/pi-cloudflare-sandbox-workflows/prototypes/shitrat-brain-proposal-ui/build"' ... git check-ignore .wzrrd/state.json -> exit 1 (not ignored); .gitignore has no .wzrrd entry.

**Fix:** Add `.wzrrd/` to .gitignore (or at minimum `.wzrrd/state.json` and `.wzrrd/workflow-run-observability-pack/` if you want to keep the .keep). If publish receipts are durable learning, capture the URLs in .brain/ instead.

### [MEDIUM] [prototypes-hygiene] shitrat-brain-proposal-ui has no .gitignore — 1.4MB of build output will be committed by the next git add

**Where:** `prototypes/shitrat-brain-proposal-ui`

The other SvelteKit spikes (system-dream-review-ui, dream-sequence-vision-ui) each carry a .gitignore covering .svelte-kit/build/node_modules, but shitrat-brain-proposal-ui has none. Its build/ (404K) and .svelte-kit/ (1.0M) directories are NOT git-ignored, and since the whole prototype is currently untracked ('?? prototypes/shitrat-brain-proposal-ui/'), `git add prototypes/` will commit generated build artifacts and the SvelteKit cache.

**Evidence:** git check-ignore results: 'NOT IGNORED: prototypes/shitrat-brain-proposal-ui/build (404K)' and 'svelte-kit NOT ignored', while prototypes/system-dream-review-ui/.gitignore contains '.svelte-kit\nbuild\nnode_modules'.

**Fix:** Copy system-dream-review-ui/.gitignore into shitrat-brain-proposal-ui (or add prototypes/**/build/ and prototypes/**/.svelte-kit/ to the root .gitignore alongside the existing prototypes/**/out/ rule). Moot if the prototype is deleted per disposition.

### [MEDIUM] [prototypes-hygiene] Three copy-pasted SvelteKit report UIs with already-diverged components — canonical copy ambiguous

**Where:** `prototypes/system-dream-review-ui/src/lib`

shitrat-brain-proposal-ui, system-dream-review-ui, and dream-sequence-vision-ui are the same Tufte report app copied three times. md5 comparison shows ReportLayout.svelte, margin-note.svelte, and pattern-cards.svelte are identical across all three, but flow-chart.svelte and stat-line.svelte have already drifted: brain-proposal-ui's copies (640651..., cb6d89...) differ from the identical pair shared by the other two (15c2d1..., 42969b...). system-dream-review-ui's own README admits the problem ('make this a package-backed workflow node, not a copied report directory') and docs/source-map.md names it the current source pattern — so a fourth copy is one dream-run away, and a fix applied to the wrong copy is silently lost.

**Evidence:** MD5 (shitrat-brain-proposal-ui/src/lib/flow-chart.svelte) = 640651a269a6a712ba6dba71637f8293 vs MD5 (system-dream-review-ui/src/lib/flow-chart.svelte) = 15c2d1dd9d9e055c20dbecd5af8139cc; system-dream-review-ui/README.md: 'the important next step is to make this a package-backed workflow node, not a copied report directory.'

**Fix:** Declare system-dream-review-ui canonical (matches docs/source-map.md), delete the other two copies after capturing their published-report receipts, and build the wzrrd.report.render workflow node from it before any further dream runs spawn copy number four.

### [MEDIUM] [prototypes-hygiene] prototypes/README.md 'Active' list omits 6 of 16 prototypes

