README says "The current route surface is `POST /runs`" and "`migrations/0001_workflow_app_d1.sql` mirrors the app D1 schema." The deployed route adapter also serves GET /runs/:runId/events (JSON/SSE/live-tail/WebSocket), GET /runs/:runId/debugger, and POST /admin/packages/{seed,prepare-seed,finalize-seed}; the D1 schema now spans three migrations (0001 plus 0002_workflow_telemetry_logs.sql and 0003_workflow_events.sql), matching the workflow_telemetry_logs and workflow_events tables in d1-schema.ts. The spine doc documents all of this, so the README is simply stale relative to it.

**Evidence:** README.md: "The current route surface is `POST /runs`. ... `migrations/0001_workflow_app_d1.sql` mirrors the app D1 schema." vs cloudflare-worker-route.ts:1230-1262: `/^\/runs\/([^/]+)\/debugger$/u`, `/^\/runs\/([^/]+)\/events$/u`, `"/admin/packages/prepare-seed"`, `"/admin/packages/finalize-seed"`, `"/admin/packages/seed"`; `ls migrations`: 0001_workflow_app_d1.sql, 0002_workflow_telemetry_logs.sql, 0003_workflow_events.sql.

